<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN TAX RECEIPTS UP 5.5 PCT IN YEAR TO FEB.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN TAX RECEIPTS UP 5.5 PCT IN YEAR TO FEB.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total Belgian fiscal receipts</p>
<p>were up 11.7 percent in February from February 1996 and up 5.5</p>
<p>percent in the first two months of 1997 from the year-ago</p>
<p>period, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>TAX RECEIPTS (in mln bfr)</p>
<p>				     Feb 97	 Feb 96     pct change</p>
<p>    Total			  157,734	141,243     11.7</p>
<p>    Direct taxation	     97,077	 61,035     59.1</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes   34,324	 34,970    - 1.8</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE TAX RECEIPTS (in mln bfr)</p>
<p>				     Jan-Feb 97   Jan-Feb 96 pct change</p>
<p>    Total			    343,703	325,646    5.5</p>
<p>    Direct taxation		205,934	167,948   22.6</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes     81,071	 80,247    1.0</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
